wordfreq 3.1.1 -- notices for the word frequencies in words-en.txt and words-fr.txt
=====================================================================================

The unigram frequencies in words-en.txt and words-fr.txt are derived from the
`large_en` and `large_fr` word lists of wordfreq 3.1.1 by Robyn Speer
(https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7199437),
taken from the wheel wordfreq-3.1.1-py3-none-any.whl on PyPI (SHA-256
4b1c6ecffc6198be3396d5cf871c4423ca71c907c231348d352dd54d62b97473).

Those data files are licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Changes made: the lists were
filtered to a vocabulary (SCOWL plus extra-en.txt for English, the
Grammalecte lexicon for French), truncated to the most frequent words, and
their centibel frequency buckets were converted to log-scaled integer
weights. The resulting tables are licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0; as a
ShareAlike adaptation they may also be used under the GNU General Public
License version 3 (CC BY-SA 4.0 lists GPLv3 as a compatible licence), which
section 13 of the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 lets Tilo
combine with its AGPL-3.0-only code.

The wordfreq code (not used here, but whose notice travels with its data) is
under the Apache License 2.0:

Copyright 2022 Robyn Speer

